openMSX configuration resources
================================

The files distributed under `server/resources/openmsx/share/` and their
source-checkout counterparts under `.openmsx-home/share/` are configuration
templates for the openMSX emulator. They include adapted machine definitions
and small documentation files based in part on material from the openMSX
project, pinned here to the openMSX 21.0 release (`RELEASE_21_0`, commit
`cb61db7`):

    https://github.com/openMSX/openMSX/tree/RELEASE_21_0

Copyright belongs to the respective openMSX authors and MSX-AI contributors.
These configuration resources are distributed under the GNU General Public
License, version 2. A copy is included as `GPL-2.0.txt` in this directory.

The machine-template source inputs are:

    share/machines/Gradiente_Expert_Plus.xml
      SHA-256 1c50edbe852374719fa4d3ffbf975653bda98b113c3edf153264b42c48e369d7
    share/machines/Sony_HB-F1XDJ.xml
      SHA-256 c7577e176780faf301a4ca1525ecb7fd0292fb8c257c778b424b568d9b6d0b17

The two Gradiente variants combine the upstream Expert identity, keyboard,
PPI, PSG, printer, and slot conventions with the upstream MSX2 engine, VDP,
RTC, and mapper configuration pattern. The two Sony variants are reduced
forms of the exact HB-F1XDJ file above. The copied documentation inputs are:

    share/extensions/README
      SHA-256 95f627b9088d69e1029f8b6bf1d25980956b4cf81dd93acfc98770fe44da85ac
    share/software/README
      SHA-256 2be4799826517cc6bf391d713fa3d280669b41e0e19d3c231678615f161d7d07

`rs232_proto.xml` and `settings.xml` are MSX-AI-authored configuration files,
distributed with the adapted/copy resources as one GPL-2.0 template set.

MSX-AI modifications, recorded no later than 2026-08-07, include reduced
machine profiles, mapper-size variants, an RS-232 test extension,
firmware-independent descriptions, and local settings used by the isolated
test environment. The complete preferred form for modification is the XML,
settings, and README source present in this repository and in the source
distribution. The MSX-AI Python implementation, Z80 agent, and
project-authored documentation are GPL-3.0-or-later except where another
bundled notice says otherwise.
